instructions:
In src/todo.js, at the text `export function loadTodos(homeDir) {
  return []
}

export function saveTodos(homeDir, todos) {}

export function addTodo(homeDir, text) {
  return null
}

export function completeTodo(homeDir, id) {
  return null
}

export function removeTodo(homeDir, id) {
  return null
}`: Add `import { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs'` above the first export. loadTodos(homeDir) must readFileSync(todosPath(homeDir), 'utf8') and return JSON.parse of it; catch only an error whose code is 'ENOENT' and return [] so a first run lists empty, but let malformed JSON throw. saveTodos(homeDir, todos) must writeFileSync(todosPath(homeDir), JSON.stringify(todos, null, 2) + '\n'). addTodo(homeDir, text) must load the current todos, compute id as Math.max(0, ...todos.map(t => t.id)) + 1, push { id, text, done: false }, save, and return the new todo. completeTodo(homeDir, id) must load, find the todo with that id, return null when there is none, otherwise set its done to true without touching the other entries, save, and return it. removeTodo(homeDir, id) must load, return null when no entry matches, otherwise splice the entry out, save, and return the removed entry.

In src/todo.js, at the text `export function formatTodos(todos, pendingOnly) {
  return ''
}`: Return one line per todo shaped as `${t.id}. ${t.done ? CHECK_MARK + ' ' : ''}${t.text}`, first dropping every entry where t.done === true when pendingOnly is truthy, then joining the lines with a single newline and returning '' when no lines remain. Use the existing CHECK_MARK constant, never a literal check mark.

In src/cli.js, at the text `export function run(argv, io) {
  return 0
}`: Add `import { addTodo, completeTodo, removeTodo, loadTodos, formatTodos } from './todo.js'` at the top. In run, destructure `const [command, ...rest] = argv` and switch on it: 'add' joins rest with a space, returns 1 after io.write('todo: add requires some text') when that text is empty, otherwise calls addTodo(io.homeDir, text) and returns 0; 'list' computes `const out = formatTodos(loadTodos(io.homeDir), rest.includes('--pending'))`, writes out and returns 0 when out is non-empty, and writes 'No todos.' and returns 0 when it is empty; 'done' validates that Number(rest[0]) is a finite integer, returning 1 after io.write('todo: done requires a numeric id') otherwise, then calls completeTodo(io.homeDir, id) and returns 1 after writing a no-such-todo message when it returns null, else returns 0; 'remove' does the same id validation and message shape against removeTodo; the default branch returns 1 after io.write('usage: todo <add|list|done|remove> ...'). Never call process.exit, and never import or call os.homedir here.

In package.json, at the text `"scripts": {
    "test": "node --test"
  }`: Insert a top-level "bin" key before "scripts" so the entry becomes `"bin": {` / `    "todo": "./bin/todo.js"` / `  },` / `  "scripts": {` / `    "test": "node --test"` / `  }`. Keep the JSON valid and leave name, type and scripts untouched.
